# Shell, Home, tenant switcher, palette, toasts

Source: `prototype/R2App.dc.html` (sidebar markup, `nav`, `switchPatch`,
`requestSwitch`, `palette*`, `toast*`, `top`, Home section). Chunk: C28 (shell,
Home skeleton), C30 (Home attention list backed by Inbox scope).

## Sidebar

- Top: tenant switcher button showing tenant name and environment pill;
  ⌘T opens the list. Entries: every tenant (name, environment, TSG), then
  "Add a tenant…". Selected tenant uses `sel/selInk`.
- Destinations in the order of DESIGN-V2 §5 with icon, label, shortcut hint.
  Unavailable destinations render disabled with their availability reason as
  a tooltip and accessible description, never hidden.
- Bottom: appearance toggle (light/dark/system) and "Show the calls" toggle,
  both dispatching their Rust preference.
- Collapses to icons below 1280px window width.

## Home

- Title "Home" with the tenant name and environment beneath; last-read line
  from `ReadStatus` ("Read finished at 07:45 · all sources complete" or
  "· 3 sources partial", warn-styled when partial; "First read pending" on a
  fresh tenant).
- "Needs attention": up to five Inbox items of kind Needs action, each with
  severity (colour + icon + word), title, product, action button that
  navigates with context, Acknowledge, and Snooze whose tooltip and
  accessible name are the item's `snoozeLabel`.
- Product cards for admitted, licensed products with their read state;
  unlicensed products are listed once as "Not licensed in this tenant" and
  unavailable products once as "Not available in this release" (DESIGN-V2
  §6), never hidden.
- Playground card (Runtime Security scan): prompt, direction, profile select,
  verdict panel (word + icon + reason + plain explanation). Verdicts are
  profile-aware: a detector not enabled, or a topic not assigned, reads "Not
  detected" with the reason; monitor-only turns Blocked into Flagged with the
  profile named.

## Tenant switch (I1, I2)

- `switchTenant{tenant_id, resolution?}`; the core refuses with
  `SwitchBlocked{pending: {conversation, decision}}` when a Harness decision is
  pending. The UI renders the guard dialog (Archive and switch / Discard and
  switch / Stay) from that payload and re-dispatches with `resolution`.
- Every entry point (switcher, palette, menu, wizard completion) uses the same
  intent. After a switch the new tenant's Home renders from cached scopes within
  100 ms with read status pending until the read lands.

## Command palette

- ⌘K. Entries: destinations from the Rust inventory, tenants, and three actions
  (Navigate, Switch tenant, Read now). Typing filters; Enter dispatches; Escape
  closes and restores focus. Native menu navigation while the palette is open
  closes it first.

## Toasts (I10)

- Kinds ok, info, warn with icon and colour; one visible at a time, newest
  replaces; 6 s expiry (persist under Reduce Motion); optional Undo action
  (snooze). A toast never carries information absent from an observed scope.

## Modals (I8)

- Stack order kept in the shell store; only the topmost is interactive;
  siblings get `aria-hidden`; Escape closes the topmost; focus returns to the
  opener. Detail sheets (transcripts, facts) are modals in this stack.

## Fixtures and tests

- Fixture boards: R2Palette, R2Tenants, R2Dark, R2App default.
- V2-T01, T02, T09, T10, T11; V2-N01, N03, N04, N05.
# First-run wizard and add-tenant sheet

Source: `prototype/R2Onboard.dc.html` (steps, `ERR`, `touch`, `vsig`,
`verify`, `opened`, `railCtx`, `mode="add"`), `R2App` `addtenant` overlay.
Chunk: C29. Realises D013 (scan-key-first onboarding).

## Steps (first run)

1. **Welcome** — explains that the app is built entirely on Palo Alto
   Networks' public APIs and exists to show application builders what those
   interfaces make possible; three cards: Built on the public APIs / See the
   calls as you go / Learn by doing. Continue.
2. **Tenant** — name, environment (select), region (select), TSG id, then
   three credential sections in this order (D013, deviation P17):
   **Scan key** (required on first run): "Add scan key…" opens the host
   secret sheet and returns a vault id shown as a masked indicator.
   **Management client** (optional): client id field plus "Add client
   secret…" (host secret sheet); without it Administration is read-only and
   says so. **Gateway** (optional toggle): workspace name, endpoint URL,
   "Add workspace key…". Secondary action "Import from Prisma AIRS Desktop
   v1" fills name/environment/TSG from the import intent; secrets are always
   re-entered. Validation per field on blur with
   `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby`; the Continue button names what is
   missing. After this step the rail shows "Name · Environment · TSG …" under
   its title.
3. **Products** — cards for the products in DESIGN-V2 §6. Admitted products
   show licence state read from the tenant and are selectable; Red Team and
   Model/skill are marked read-only; Agentic Identity Security and Agentic
   Endpoint Security are shown as "Not available in this release" and cannot
   be selected (P18).
4. **Verify** — dispatch `verifyTenantSetup`; per-product rows fill as
   `VerifyStep` results stream (pass / warning / fail with reason) using the
   existing reads for each admitted product (scan capability check, a
   management read when a client is present, Gateway prerequisites).
   Unavailable products show "Not available", never a result. The warning
   and failed rows are fixtures on admitted products. Fail offers "Fix and verify
   again" (returns to Tenant) or "Continue with warnings"; warnings become
   Inbox items on completion.
5. **Starter packs** (optional) — test-case packs per selected product with
   counts.
6. **Academy account** (optional) — sign in or skip; the trust copy states
   exactly what syncs (Academy progress only).
7. **Done** — summary; "Open Prisma AIRS" is finite (`opening` → done) and
   dispatches `completeOnboarding`.

## Add-tenant sheet (`mode="add"`)

- 1160×780 sheet over the shell, rail 244px, no Welcome or Academy steps,
  Cancel at every step; completion dispatches `addTenant` then `switchTenant`.
  Cancel discards everything except a credential already written by the
  secret sheet, which is shown in Administration as unattached and can be
  removed there.

## Core contract

- `verifyTenantSetup{draft}` → stream of `VerifyStep{product, state, reason}`
  then `VerifyDone{warnings}`.
- `completeOnboarding{name, env, region, tsg, scan_credential_id,
  management: {client_id, credential_id}?, gateway: {ws, endpoint,
  credential_id}?, products, packs, academy_opt_in, warnings}` writes the tenant profile, product
  selection, packs and Inbox warning items; sets `onboarding=done`.
- `addTenant{...same minus academy}`.
- The core never receives a secret through these intents; `credential_ids`
  reference vault records created by the host secret sheet.

## Fixtures and tests

- Boards: see [boards.md](boards.md) (`fx.on.*`, `fx.addTenant`).
- Tests: step validation and invalidation signature; streaming verify order;
  cancel semantics; `onboarding` transitions; V2-N02.
- Live (C29 only): verify against Vulture, reads only, under the designated
  scope.
# Inbox and reads

Source: `R2App` (`ITEMS`, `visibleItems`, `ack`, `snoozed`, `snooze`,
`inboxRows`, `sel`, `startRead`, `recheck`, `toGo`). Chunk: C30.

## Inbox

- Tabs All / Needs action / Updates / Snoozed with counts. Rows: severity
  (colour + icon + word), title, product, source line ("API keys · cached",
  "rotated 07:46"), when, acknowledged mark. Selecting opens the detail pane:
  body, facts table, "Why this matters" explanation, action button (navigates
  with context), Acknowledge / Mark as needing action, Snooze or Unsnooze.
- Empty states distinguish "first read pending" from "nothing needs action"
  and name partial sources ("3 of 6 sources were read at 07:45").
- Snooze: per item, core-computed return time, 24 hours for every item in
  P09 (the prototype's deadline-bound rotation snooze is not carried: no
  admitted operation has a grace deadline, P20). The label, toast and
  Snoozed-tab "Returns …" text all state the same time (I11). The
  `deadline` field stays optional for a future item that has a real one.
- Contextual navigation: an item's action carries a target (screen, product,
  tab, conversation). Into an ended conversation it sets a transient hint
  offering "Open the saved transcript" and "Start a new investigation".

## Reads (I4)

- `readTenant` runs a finite read of every selected product; `ReadStatus`
  carries per-product state (pending, ok, partial, needsRole), last-read
  time and counts. First read on a fresh tenant shows pending everywhere.
- Completion toast: ok "Read finished at 07:45 · all sources complete" or
  warn "· 3 sources partial"; for fresh tenants "· 1 product still needs a
  role" or "· no activity yet in <tenant>". `recheckProduct` after a role is
  granted shows an info toast and re-reads.

## Core contract

- Scope `InboxItem{id, kind, severity, title, product, source, when, body,
  facts, action_target, explanation, deadline?, snooze_return?, acknowledged}`
  per tenant; intents `acknowledgeItem`, `snoozeItem`, `unsnoozeItem`,
  `readTenant`, `recheckProduct`.
- The rotation reminder (`rotation-<application>`) is a distinct item id from
  the expiry alert and clears only when the old key's deletion is read back
  (I7). Items exist only for admitted products (DESIGN-V2 §6).

## Fixtures and tests

- Board R2Inbox. Tests V2-R02, R04, R08, R09; V2-T04, T12, T13; V2-N02.
# Harness

Source: `R2App` (`CONVOS` blocks/mcp/keys at lines 760–790, `decs`, `ended`,
`archiveActive`, `sendDraft`, `startNewConvo`, `convoHint`, `follows`),
boards R2Harness, R2Harness2, R2Harness3. Chunk: C32.

The screen is a re-skin of the existing Harness engine, sessions, decisions,
MCP and sign-in modules (C19–C22); the conversation, decision and project
authority model is unchanged. D014's Harness restrictions hold: a proposal
never authorises Apply.

## Layout

- Title row "Harness" with tenant and engine status; left rail of
  conversations (lifecycle seeds appear only on non-fresh fixture tenants;
  user conversations titled from their first message; archived ones marked
  ended); main transcript; composer with a draft per conversation.
- Prerequisites checklist (tenant, management client, Gateway workspace,
  company sign-in) stays visible until satisfied (D057 F05).

## Lifecycles (fixture conversations)

All three are **read-only** tool-call lifecycles in the prototype; none
writes to a tenant from the Harness.

1. **blocks** — "Why were 14 prompts blocked on claims-triage overnight?":
   read-only tool call `list_security_events` (in-page Approve once /
   Decline), result summary, recommendation, follow-up "Open the review"
   that opens the injection-override topic review in Administration
   (Runtime Security, `ChangeKind::Topics`).
2. **mcp** — "Which laptops run an MCP server that is not on the allow
   list?": in the prototype the read-only call targets an AES inventory.
   AES has no admitted service (DESIGN-V2 §6), so the implemented fixture
   reads the workspace MCP server inventory the core already exposes
   (`GatewayRead::McpServers`, C22) and its follow-up opens a Gateway
   guardrail review (`ChangeKind::GatewayGuardrails`). Recorded as
   deviation P16.
3. **keys** — "Which API keys expire before the audit, and can you rotate
   them?": read-only key inventory; the Harness refuses to rotate ("rotation
   is a write; it goes through Administration and a review") and hands off
   to the key rotation flow. The follow-up text reflects the rotation stage
   (additional key issued / old key removed).

Each has approve, decline, end and follow-up paths. Declining records the
decision and the assistant's declined text; ending seals the session
(`endConversation` → archive id) and the rail shows it ended.

Tool-call approval stays as C21/C22 built it: the core decides from the
tool's write flag whether the host's native confirmation sheet is required;
read-only calls use the in-page bar. No P09 fixture exercises a write-capable
call; the native sheet path is covered by the existing C21 tests.

## Rules

- A fresh tenant's first send creates a user conversation (I12); sending in
  an ended conversation creates a new one.
- Contextual navigation into an ended conversation shows a hint with "Open
  the saved transcript" (archived transcript detail) and "Start a new
  investigation" (new conversation prefilled with the opening question). The
  hint clears on any navigation.
- A pending decision blocks tenant switch (I1).

## Fixtures and tests

- Boards R2Harness (blocks), R2Harness2 (mcp), R2Harness3 (keys). Tests
  V2-R01, V2-T01, T13; V2-T17 approve/decline/end/follow-up per lifecycle;
  V2-T18 the keys lifecycle never dispatches a mutation from the Harness.

